<title>COLOMBIA: Nine foreign firms in Colombia generators bidding.</title>
<headline>Nine foreign firms in Colombia generators bidding.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine companies, all foreign, qualified for the bidding for seven Colombian power plants, an official said Thursday.</p>
<p>The companies are Enron, AES Hydro Inc. and KLT Power, of the United States, Chilenger, through its subsidiary Energy Trade and Finance Coproration, and Endesa, of Chile, National Power Plc, of Britain, Steag Atkiengesellschaft, of Germany, Iberdola y Endesa, of Spain, and Electricidad de Caracas, of Venezuela.</p>
<p>The Colombian government is hoping to raise $1.1 billion with the sale of the seven power generators, the largest of which is the 1,000 megawatt Chivor plant.  </p>
<p>The winning bids are due to be announced on Dec. 19 or 20, said Juan Fernando Bonilla who is heading the privatization process.</p>
<p>-- Karl Penhaul, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
